I hold many journeys still, though I never travel away;
Two-wheelers and cars wait here through much of the day.
Before you walk to class, your ride may rest with mine;
Find the place where vehicles stand in a line.

Where am I?

People enter through me and leave the same way;
I mark the campus boundary at the start of the day.
Visitors look for me, and students pass through in a stream;
Find the main entrance that leads into the college scene.

Where am I?

I am not a bank teller, yet I can provide cash;
A card and a secret number help make the transaction flash.
When your wallet is light, I may be your call;
Find the machine that lets you withdraw it all.

Where am I?

I send water upward, then watch it fall;
In sunlight, tiny droplets can sparkle for all.
I make a gentle sound but never leave my place;
Find the water feature that brings movement to the space.

Where am I?

Future managers study leadership and business inside;
Look for the entrance where their classes reside.
The building is known as LC1, so use that name as your guide;
Find the main gate to the MBA block on this side.

Where am I?

Here, tools and ideas work together side by side;
Things may be built or fixed, tested, changed, or tried.
It is where practical skills grow stronger than before;
Find the place where hands-on learning opens a door.

Where should you go?

